# Deploy Updates Rule

Whenever you make updates to the codebase and the user asks to finalize or deploy, or if the update fixes a primary user request, you MUST routinely test on the cloud by pushing the code to git and deploying to Firebase by following the `/deploy` workflow found in `.agents/workflows/deploy.md`.

You should:
1. Stage and commit changes (using git add and git commit).
2. Push to GitHub with `git push origin main`.
3. Check what was changed and run the appropriate `npx firebase-tools deploy` command (or `firebase deploy` if installed globally) as specified in the `/deploy` workflow so that changes are available on the cloud.

# General execution rules
- Ask any questions you have.
- Do not guess.
- Do not assume.
